# SBOB-EXAMPLES DEMO WATERMARK — synthetic auditd corpus, scenario A (M3,
# issue #4). Not captured telemetry: the reconstruction's observer model,
# synthetic inode/pid/timestamp fields; every path mirrors the M1
# reconstruction's actual collection lists (docs/agent-framework/
# incident-map.md). The exfil endpoint is the loopback-only sink standing in
# for webhook[.]site (TDS §4); port 8099 is the reconstruction's sink default.
#
# Drift window: the FIRST interpreter start after the malicious release is
# installed (the .pth hook fires with zero test reachability). Expected fired
# rule ids (band = slot 2, sbobs/registry.yaml):
#   100221  open drift    — /proc/*/environ sweep + credential-file reads:
#                          nothing outside site-packages, the repo checkout
#                          and resolv.conf is a declared open
#   100231  connect drift — the single exfil POST to the sink (undeclared peer)
# Honest absences (asserted by the lane, the finding is the point):
#   100211  exec drift stays QUIET: the stealer lives INSIDE the declared
#          interpreter (fork + daemon thread, no execve) — unlike php2shell,
#          where the shell exec fires. Mode A exe-scoping keys the malicious
#          process because the interpreter itself is the compromised exe.
#   100201  sensitive-file overlay stays QUIET: the stealer's cloud
#          credential set (.azure/, .npmrc, .git-credentials, runner tokens)
#          is NOT on the sensitive-file watchlist (shadow/sudoers/.ssh/
#          id_rsa) — the cloud-credential watchlist gap, M2 finding 3's
#          roadmap ask, recorded in docs/agent-framework/runtime-evidence.md.
#   100222/100232 sustained children stay QUIET in the single pass: the real
#          stealer reads MANY files but connects EXACTLY ONCE (single-POST,
#          no-retry semantics). Sustained capability is proven on the
#          synthetic repetition corpus (sustained.audit).
#   The DNS leg is QUIET on purpose: resolving the exfil domain rides the
#          declared resolver (TDS §9.3 DNS-blind limitation) — the CONNECT to
#          the resolved sink IP is what alerts.

